  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0010","idiomatic","His son Zheng Jing renamed the Eastern Capital Dongning Province and elevated the two counties to prefecture rank.","His son Zheng Jing renamed the Eastern Capital Dongning Province and elevated the two counties to departments.","s0010 states 升二縣為州: the two counties are raised to 州 (departments), not 府 (prefectures). Adjacent s0009 and s0011 reserve 府 for Chengtian/Taiwan prefectures, so 'prefecture rank' misranks the elevation; 'departments' matches 州.","high","applied"],
    ["s0028","idiomatic","Between Jiayi to the east and Zhanghua to the south, from the Zhuoshui River to the Gushigui River—a district of roughly four hundred li—we propose a new Yunlin County.","East of Jiayi and south of Zhanghua, from the Zhuoshui River to the Gushigui River—a district of roughly four hundred li—we propose a new Yunlin County.","s0028 reads 嘉義之東，彰化之南: east of Jiayi and south of Zhanghua. 'Between Jiayi to the east and Zhanghua to the south' garbles the two directional genitives; the proposed wording restores both.","high","applied"],
    ["s0037","idiomatic","We propose Taitung Directly Subordinate Prefecture, bounded by Yilan on the west and Hengchun on the east—over five hundred li long and ten to forty li wide—still under the Taiwan military intendant.","We propose Taitung Directly Subordinate Prefecture, bounded on the left by Yilan and on the right by Hengchun—over five hundred li long and ten to forty li wide—still under the Taiwan military intendant.","s0037 has 左界宜蘭，右界恆春: left and right bounds are Yilan and Hengchun. Mapping these to west and east invents cardinal directions the Chinese does not give; preserving left/right is accurate.","high","applied"],
    ["s0048","idiomatic","It lies seven thousand two hundred fifty li northwest of the capital.","The capital is seven thousand two hundred fifty li to the northwest.","s0048's 西北距京師七千二百五十里 places the capital 7,250 li northwest of the province; this wording preserves that orientation in natural English.","high","applied"],
    ["s0104","idiomatic","It lay two hundred li northeast of the provincial capital.","The provincial capital lay two hundred li to the northeast.","s0104's 東北距省治二百里 places the provincial capital 200 li northeast of Tainan Prefecture; this wording preserves that orientation in natural English.","high","applied"],
    ["s0153","idiomatic","It lay three hundred fifty li southwest of the provincial capital.","The provincial capital lay three hundred fifty li to the southwest.","s0153's 西南距省治三百五十里 places the provincial capital 350 li southwest of Taipei Prefecture; this wording preserves that orientation in natural English.","high","applied"],
    ["s0189","idiomatic","It lay five hundred li northwest of the provincial capital.","The provincial capital lay five hundred li to the northwest.","s0189's 西北距省治五百里 places the provincial capital 500 li northwest of Taitung; this wording preserves that orientation in natural English.","high","applied"]
  ],
